Q1. What is a Package in PL/SQL?

Interview Ready Answer

A Package is a database object that groups related procedures,
functions, variables, cursors and exceptions into a single unit.

Packages are used to organize business logic, improve code
reusability and simplify maintenance.

Purpose

• Group related PL/SQL objects.
• Improve modularity.
• Increase code reusability.
• Simplify maintenance.
• Improve security.

======================================================================

Q2. Why do we need Packages?

Interview Ready Answer

Packages are used to organize related PL/SQL components into a
single database object.

Advantages

• Better code organization.
• Code reusability.
• Easier maintenance.
• Improved modularity.
• Better security.
• Better performance because the package is loaded once into memory.

======================================================================

Q3. What are the Parts of a Package?

Interview Ready Answer

A PL/SQL Package consists of two parts.

1. Package Specification
2. Package Body

======================================================================

Q4. What is Package Specification?

Interview Ready Answer

Package Specification is the public interface of a package.

It contains the declarations of procedures, functions, variables,
cursors and exceptions that are accessible from outside the package.

Purpose

• Declares package members.
• Defines public interface.
• Does not contain implementation.

======================================================================

Q5. What is Package Body?

Interview Ready Answer

Package Body contains the implementation of the procedures and
functions declared in the Package Specification.

Purpose

• Contains executable code.
• Implements declared procedures and functions.
• Can also contain private procedures and functions that are not
  accessible outside the package.

======================================================================

Q6. Difference between Package Specification and Package Body.

Interview Ready Answer

Package Specification

• Contains declarations.
• Public interface.
• Accessible from outside.
• No implementation.

------------------------------------------------------------

Package Body

• Contains implementation.
• Executable code.
• Can contain private members.
• Implements Specification.

