QUESTION 4 : What is a Repository in Git?
====================================================================

Interview Ready Answer

A Git repository is a project managed by Git. It contains the
project files along with a hidden .git directory, which stores
commit history, branch information, configuration, and metadata
required for version control.

Definition

Repository = Project + .git folder

Purpose

• Stores project source code
• Stores commit history
• Stores branch information
• Stores Git configuration
• Enables version control

Important Keywords

• Project managed by Git
• .git folder
• Commit History
• Branches
• Metadata

Memory Trick

Project + .git = Git Repository

Without .git = Normal Folder

